## Responsive Design

### Mobile-First Approach
- **Base styles**: Mobile-first
- **Breakpoints**: `md:` for desktop (768px+)
- **Container**: `max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4`

### Responsive Text
```typescript
// Responsive headings
className="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800"

// Responsive buttons
className="w-7 h-7 md:w-8 md:h-8"
```

## Animation Patterns

### Framer Motion
```typescript
// Fade in with delay
<motion.div
  initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 20 }}
  animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
  transition={{ duration: 0.5, delay: 0.1 }}
>

// Expand/collapse
<motion.div
  initial={{ opacity: 0, height: 0 }}
  animate={{ opacity: 1, height: 'auto' }}
  exit={{ opacity: 0, height: 0 }}
>
```

## Loading States

### Spinner Pattern
```typescript
<div className="flex items-center justify-center py-12">
  <div className="animate-spin rounded-full h-8 w-8 border-b-2 border-blue-600"></div>
  <span className="ml-3 text-gray-600">Loading...</span>
</div>
```

### Error States
```typescript
<div className="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg p-4 mb-6">
  <p className="text-red-800">Error message</p>
  <button className="mt-2 text-red-600 hover:text-red-800 underline">
    Try again
  </button>
</div>
```

## Development Guidelines

### Adding New Forms
1. Use consistent input field styling with `text-gray-900`
2. Include appropriate icons for each field
3. Implement real-time validation with error clearing
4. Add proper loading and error states
5. Test responsive behavior on mobile and desktop

### Form Validation
1. Clear errors when user starts typing
2. Show specific validation messages
3. Prevent form submission with invalid data
4. Maintain user input during validation

### Accessibility
1. Use proper labels for all form fields
2. Include ARIA attributes where needed
3. Ensure keyboard navigation works
4. Test with screen readers
